(14687,'Elisha De Garis','Elisha De Garis Clement: Born 17 September 1851, St Martin, Guernsey, Channel Islands \nEducation: Collegiate School of St Peter, Adelaide \nCareer: Architect (Crouch and Wilson, Melbourne); Methodist minister (1876–1887); Founding chairman, Tragowel Plains Irrigation and Water Supply Trust; Chairman, Central Irrigation League; Founder and editor, Australian Irrigationist; Commissioner, Melbourne Centennial International Exhibition; Businessman (auctioneer, real estate agent, dried-fruits broker, financier, Mildura); Member, Mildura Shire Council (President 1907–08); Dried-fruit agency operator (Melbourne) \nDied: 2 July 1948, Geelong, Victoria'),
