(14702,'Ernest Henshaw','Ernest Percival Henshaw (1870-1950): Elected 1904 \nBorn: 4 September 1870, Geelong, Victoria \nCareer: Apprenticed as a carpenter, emigrated to Western Australia in 1894. \nActive in the labour movement, elected to the WA Legislative Assembly seat of Collie in 1904. \nDefeated in 1905, held various Labor Party positions, and contested the federal seat of Perth in 1910. \nForeman carpenter for Henderson Naval Base during WWI, later a building surveyor. \nHelped form the Institute of Quantity Surveyors in the late 1930s. Rejoined the Labor Party in 1947. \nDied: 11 June 1950, Subiaco.'),
