(34049,'John Henry Kelly','John Henry Kelly: Born 17 May 1895, Hornsby, Sydney, Australia.\nEducation: Good Samaritan Convent School, Campbelltown; Christian Brothers’ School, Lewisham; St Joseph’s College, Hunters Hill.\nCareer: Conveyor-belt operator at Darling Harbour wheat terminal; General hand for a well-boring contractor; Abattoir worker; Sapper and driver in the Australian Imperial Force during World War I; Farmer in the Murrumbidgee Irrigation Area; President of Wade Shire Council; Clerk in the Royal Australian Air Force during World War II; Member of the Department of Post-War Reconstruction and Bureau of Agricultural Economics; Consultant in northern Australian beef cattle industry; Author and researcher on northern development.\nDied: 9 April 1983, Canberra.'),
