(34753,'Thomas John Ley','Thomas John Ley: Born October 28, 1880 in Bath, Somerset, England.\nMoved to Sydney, 1886. Studied under a solicitor and became one in 1914.\nAlderman on Hurstville Council, 1907.\nMLA for Hurstville, 1917.\nNSW Minister for Justice, 1922.\nFederal Member for Barton, 1925.\nReturned to England, 1928.\nFound guilty of murder in England, 1946.\nDied at Broadmoor Asylum on July 24, 1947.\nSee also:\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cMIyRxhU4CQ'),
