(42306,'Patrick Currie','Patrick Currie (1883-1949): Born on 2 August 1883 at Petrie Creek, near Caboolture, Queensland, Australia. \nEducation: Nambour State School. \nCareer: Teacher with the Queensland Education Department; Lieutenant in the cadets; Major in the Australian Imperial Force; \nSecond-in-command of the 26th Battalion; Commander of \'A\' Company, 26th Battalion; Commander of the 7th Training Brigade; \nCommander of the 28th Battalion; Commander of the 42nd Battalion in the militia; Headmaster of New Farm primary school in Brisbane; \nAssistant officer in charge of troops on various troopships during World War II. \nDied: 6 January 1949 from heart disease in Toombul, Brisbane, and buried in the Catholic section of Lutwyche cemetery.'),
