(42329,'W Forgan Smith','William Forgan Smith (1887-1953): Elected 1915, 1918, 1920, 1923, 1926, 1929, 1932, 1935, 1938 Resigned 9 December 1942: see by-election \nLater career: Chairman, Sugar Board and Central Sugar Cane Prices  Board. \nChancellor, University of Queensland. \nDied 23 September 1953 \n-------------------------------------------------------------------- \nPremier to 16 September 1942 \nChief Secretary to 16 September 1942 \nTreasurer to 12 April 1938 \nMinister without Portfolio to 9 December 1942 \nLeader of the Labor Party to 9 September 1942\n -------------------------------------------------------------------- \nSmith resigned partly through ill-health and partly because he  (rightly) believed that the federal uniform tax acts of 1942 \"would  reduce the States to a condition of penurious dependence on the  Federal government.\" (ADB) At his resignation he was the longest- serving Premier of Queensland.'),
