(42356,'Henry Buchanan','Henry Buchanan: Born 14 July, 1889, Gympie, Queensland.\nCareer: Miner before enlisting on 27 August 1914. \nServed as a stretcher bearer in Gallipoli, wounded multiple times. \nPromoted to Corporal in March 1916, then Sergeant in September 1916. \nAwarded the Military Medal and Bar for actions at Mouquet Farm and Pozieres.\nRe-enlisted in July 1918, discharged in December 1918 with multiple wounds. \nMarried Gwen Gilpin on 14 August 1920. \nLater moved to Tewantin, served as RSL President. \nDied on 11 May 1953.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n'),
