(44978,'Ron Withnall   Brian Manning','Ronald John Withnall: Born 9 September 1914, Townsville, Queensland\nEducation: Canterbury High School, Sydney; University of Sydney (Law)\nCareer: Crown Law Officer, Northern Territory; First President, Northern Territory Law Society (1968); Member, Northern Territory Legislative Council (1960–1974); Member, Northern Territory Legislative Assembly (1974–1977)\nDied: 16 September 1990\n\nBrian Thomas Manning: Born 13 October 1932, Mundubbera, Queensland\nEducation: Brisbane High School\nCareer: Trade unionist; Secretary, Northern Territory branch of the Waterside Workers’ Federation of Australia; Co-founder, Northern Territory Trades and Labor Council\nDied: 3 November 2013\n\nWithnall was the successful candidate in the 1974 election for Port Darwin.'),
